  "description": "We are converting the commercial unit into one apartment. the flat has been mistakenly labeled as two units instead of one, most likely because of its name Unit 4a&b. When we purchased the unit in December 2023 from Savills it was listed as one unit. Please find that attached in addendum too. You will see by the proposed and existing plans that the space has never been divided into two separate units on the plans. it has been one open space. Please refer to the attached plans and list of renovations below for a complete overview\n\nPlease see attached document \"Warple\". \n\nNoted also as below:\n\nSPECIFICATION FOR PROPOSED INTERNAL ALTERATIONS\nInsulation Provide 30mm backed plasterboard ton all external walls\nKitchen wc / bath\nBoiler Waste\nElectrical\nDoors Bedroom\nStudding WC / bath\nStudding Bedroom\nensure mechanical is provided extraction externally vented / 30l/s provide 15l/s external extraction\nExisting vents appear to exist in service cupboard. To be confirmed\nIf new boiler required, to meet sebduk rating requirements\nAll new waste to be linked to existing SVP in riser cupboard\nAll new pipework to kitchen and bathroom to be UPVC 38dia\nprovided with 75 deep seal traps and rodding eyes at all elbows.\nWC 100 dia UPVC linked to existing SVP with rodding eyes at all elbows\nAll electrical work to meet Part P, designed, installed, inspected\nand tested by a person to do so. Prior to completion the council to\nbe satisfied compliance with Part P which may require a relevant\nBS7671 electrical installation certificate to be issued by a qualified electrician\nExisting fire doors to be retained All new doors to meet 1/2 hr FR\nStudding to wc and bathroom where low ceiling occurs.\nProvide 100 x 50 @ 400c/c with 12.5mm p/bd and skim\nProvide noggins below studwork running parallel with existing floor timbers Existing floor timbers 225 x 50 @ 400c/c\nStudding to bedroom where studding meets existing open pitched roof Provide 150m x 50 @ 400c/c faced in ply and 12.5mm P / bd\nTo be secured to timber header plate secured to rafters\nat head of stud for restraint\nRoof To underside of existing rafters provide additional 100mm celotex Ensure battens are secured to underside and 12.5mm plasterboard\nExpose underside of existing roof to establish existing construction ( ventilation and insulation )",
